  "transcript": [
    {
      "approx_t": 0,
      "text": "One photo, one region edited. Only her mouth was edited. Look how much of her changed. Lips are not just a feature. They are what the lower third is measured from."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 12,
      "text": "Here is every pixel that moved. Almost all of it is the mouth. Almost none of it is anywhere else."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 19,
      "text": "One. The gap under her nose. Thin lips make it long. Full lips, short. Same nose."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 28,
      "text": "Two. Another face, same edit. Same result."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 33,
      "text": "Three. Her chin looks stronger. It is the same chin. You are reading it against a new mouth."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 42,
      "text": "None of this means fuller is better. It means lips are load-bearing."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 46,
      "text": "Test it yourself. Roll your lips inward and hold. Watch your chin arrive."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 52,
      "text": "If you are about to change something there, see it on your own face first. A preview, not a promise. Search Refina AI."
    }
  ],
